This project was inspired by these MIT-licensed projects:

- https://github.com/mattpocock/skills
- https://github.com/igoruehara/spec-driven
- https://github.com/obra/superpowers
- https://github.com/backnotprop/pstack (mirror of cursor/plugins/pstack)
- https://github.com/dkubb/skills

The direction of groundwork's verification work - that a spec-driven harness is
only as good as the agent's ability to prove its own output, rather than assert
it - comes from two articles by lauren (@poteto):

- The Complete Guide to pstack Pt. 1
  https://x.com/poteto/article/2094457600259842065
- The Complete Guide to pstack Pt. 2
  https://x.com/poteto/article/2097732320606507506

The commit discipline inside a slice - verify the foundation before starting,
keep each commit whole, reduce before adding, and correct with a fixup rather
than an amend - is adapted from the atomic-changes skill by Dan Kubb (@dkubb):

- https://github.com/dkubb/skills/blob/main/skills/atomic-changes/SKILL.md
- https://x.com/dkubb/status/2097026178934800748

groundwork adapts all of those ideas onto its own artifact model rather than
vendoring any of that work. The multi-runtime install boundary follows the approach taken
by https://github.com/michael-denyer/pstack-claude.
